* Pin-named definitions of the cells that the chipalooza_frame schematic
* instantiates as xschem PRIMITIVES and that have no other netlist to read.
* A primitive binds POSITIONALLY, so the pin order here is the symbol's,
* and the names are those used on the structural (Verilog) side.
* Read into circuit 2 before the schematic;  see the Makefile.

* SPI and clock pad loopbacks.  The names are made up here and in
* gen_blackboxes.py;  setup.tcl permutes them, as a resistor is symmetric.
.subckt rm2 PLUS MINUS
.ends

